    {
      "id": "s02",
      "type": "UV_STAGE",
      "transition": "dip",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "I asked for rich and uv installed fifteen point zero. But read what it wrote to the file. Not equals. Greater than or equal to. That is a floor, not a pin.",
      "data": {
        "uvStage": {
          "layout": "terminal",
          "color": "orange",
          "headline": "Read the [operator]",
          "premise": "uv wrote a lower bound derived from what it installed, not an exact version.",
          "promptLabel": "you@laptop",
          "cwd": "~/work/invoice-app",
          "highlight": ">=",
          "steps": [
            {
              "label": "uv add rich",
              "out": [
                "Installed 5 packages in 980ms",
                " + rich==15.0.0"
              ],
              "detail": "installed exactly 15.0.0",
              "atWord": 4.083
            },
            {
              "label": "grep -A2 dependencies pyproject.toml",
              "out": [
                "dependencies = [",
                "    \"rich>=15.0.0\",",
                "]"
              ],
              "detail": "but wrote a floor, not that number",
              "atWord": 12.167
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 333,
      "audio": "audio/uv-07-short_s02.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s03",
      "type": "UV_STAGE",
      "transition": "morph",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "That is deliberate. pyproject says what your project can live with. The exact version goes in the lockfile instead, which is what your colleague actually gets.",
      "data": {
        "uvStage": {
          "kind": "constraint-line",
          "color": "blue",
          "headline": "A floor is a [wider] promise",
          "premise": "pyproject says what you can live with. The exact version is recorded elsewhere.",
          "stageTitle": "why not pin here",
          "token": "the lockfile pins it",
          "promptLabel": "you@laptop",
          "cwd": "~/work/invoice-app",
          "steps": [
            {
              "label": "grep rich pyproject.toml uv.lock",
              "out": [
                "pyproject.toml:    \"rich>=15.0.0\",",
                "uv.lock:version = \"15.0.0\""
              ],
              "detail": "the range here, the exact one there",
              "atWord": 10.667
            }
          ],
          "stage": [
            {
              "label": "rich",
              "sub": "14.0, 15.0, 15.1, 16.0, 17.0",
              "atWord": 3.25
            },
            {
              "label": "a pin would say",
              "text": "0.28..0.34",
              "detail": "==15.0.0",
              "value": 0,
              "atWord": 7.417
            },
            {
              "label": "uv wrote",
              "text": "0.28..1.00",
              "detail": ">=15.0.0",
              "atWord": 12.333
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 277,
      "audio": "audio/uv-07-short_s03.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s04",
      "type": "UV_STAGE",
      "transition": "zoom",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "And run uv tree on a real project. Look at pygments — it appears twice. Once because rich needs it, once because pytest does. Two packages asking, one copy installed.",
      "data": {
        "uvStage": {
          "kind": "shelf-share",
          "color": "purple",
          "headline": "pygments appears [twice]",
